{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; for f in /AGENTS.md /private/AGENTS.md /private/tmp/AGENTS.md; do if [ -f \"$f\" ]; then cat \"$f\"; fi; done; cat README.md ledgerly/io/csv_import.py ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py ledgerly/core/money.py ledgerly/core/transactions.py ledgerly/core/journal.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; for f in /AGENTS.md /private/AGENTS.md /private/tmp/AGENTS.md; do if [ -f \"$f\" ]; then cat \"$f\"; fi; done; cat README.md ledgerly/io/csv_import.py ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py ledgerly/core/money.py ledgerly/core/transactions.py ledgerly/core/journal.py'","aggregated_output":"# ledgerly\n\nA small personal ledger (Python 3.11+, standard library only). Import bank statements, have them\ncategorised by rules, and report income, expenses and balances per month.\n\n```bash\npython -m ledgerly account add checking \"Joint account\" --iban \"NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00\"\npython -m ledgerly import march.csv --format rabo --account checking\npython -m ledgerly report income 2026-03 --compare\npython -m ledgerly report balance\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\nStatement formats: `generic`, `ing` and `rabo` (see `ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`). Foreign\ncurrencies are converted with the rates in `rates.csv` (`date,currency,rate`). The ledger is one\nJSON file (`ledger.json`).\n\nImporting never drops or invents money: a statement line that cannot be read stops the import with\nan error naming the file and line, and nothing from that file is added.\n\"\"\"Importing a statement file into the journal: read, categorise, de-duplicate.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport io\nfrom collections.abc import Iterator\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.journal import Journal\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.io.bank_formats import DELIMITERS, READERS, Row\nfrom ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n\nENCODINGS = (\"utf-8-sig\", \"cp1252\")\nMAX_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ImportResult:\n    source: str\n    read: int = 0\n    added: int = 0\n    duplicates: int = 0\n    uncategorised: int = 0\n    warnings: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    def summary(self) -> str:\n        parts = [f\"{self.added} added\", f\"{self.duplicates} already there\"]\n        if self.uncategorised:\n            parts.append(f\"{self.uncategorised} uncategorised\")\n        return f\"{self.source}: {self.read} read, \" + \", \".join(parts)\n\n\ndef decode(data: bytes, source: str) -> str:\n    for encoding in ENCODINGS:\n        try:\n            return data.decode(encoding)\n        except UnicodeDecodeError:\n            continue\n    raise ImportError_(\"the file is neither UTF-8 nor Windows-1252 text\", source=source)\n\n\ndef rows(text: str, delimiter: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Row]:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\"), delimiter=delimiter)\n    if not reader.fieldnames:\n        raise ImportError_(\"the file is empty\", source=source)\n    for row in reader:\n        if None in row:\n            raise ImportError_(\n                f\"{len(row[None])} more field(s) than the header\", source=source, line=reader.line_num\n            )\n        if not any((value or \"\").strip() for value in row.values()):\n            continue\n        yield reader.line_num, {k.strip(): (v or \"\") for k, v in row.items() if k}\n\n\ndef read_statement(path: Path, fmt: str, account: str) -> list[Transaction]:\n    if fmt not in READERS:\n        raise ImportError_(f\"unknown format {fmt!r} (use {', '.join(READERS)})\", source=path.name)\n    try:\n        data = path.read_bytes()\n    except OSError:\n        raise ImportError_(\"cannot read the file\", source=path.name) from None\n    if len(data) > MAX_BYTES:\n        raise ImportError_(\"the file is larger than 20 MB\", source=path.name)\n    text = decode(data, path.name)\n    return list(READERS[fmt](rows(text, DELIMITERS[fmt], path.name), account, path.name))\n\n\ndef import_statement(\n    journal: Journal, path: Path, fmt: str, account: str, categorizer: Categorizer\n) -> ImportResult:\n    \"\"\"Add the statement's transactions to ``journal`` (all of them, or none on an error).\"\"\"\n\n    result = ImportResult(source=path.name)\n    transactions = read_statement(path, fmt, account)\n    result.read = len(transactions)\n    known = {t.currency for t in transactions} - {journal.chart.get(account).currency}\n    if known:\n        result.warnings.append(\n            f\"{path.name} has amounts in {', '.join(sorted(known))}; reports convert them\"\n        )\n    categorised = []\n    for transaction in transactions:\n        category = categorizer.category_for(transaction)\n        if category == \"uncategorised\":\n            result.uncategorised += 1\n        categorised.append(transaction.categorised(category))\n    result.added, result.duplicates = journal.extend(categorised)\n    return result\n\"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n\nEvery reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\nyields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n\n- ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n  sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n- ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n  ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n  comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n- ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n  dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n  ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.util.dates import parse_bank_date\nfrom ledgerly.util.text import squash, strip_reference\n\nRow = tuple[int, dict[str, str]]\nReader = Callable[[Iterable[Row], str, str], Iterator[Transaction]]\n\n# 1.234,56 or 12,50 with an optional minus: how Dutch banks write amounts.\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n\n\ndef parse_amount(text: str, *, decimal_comma: bool) -> Decimal | None:\n    \"\"\"The amount in a statement cell, or ``None`` when the cell holds no amount.\n\n    ``decimal_comma``: ``1.234,56`` (Dutch banks); otherwise ``1234.56``.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    cleaned = text.strip().replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n    if not cleaned:\n        return None\n    if decimal_comma:\n        if not EURO_AMOUNT.match(cleaned):\n            return None\n        return Decimal(cleaned.replace(\".\", \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"))\n    try:\n        value = Decimal(cleaned.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n    except InvalidOperation:\n        return None\n    return value if value.is_finite() else None\n\n\ndef _field(row: dict[str, str], name: str, source: str, line: int) -> str:\n    if name not in row or row[name] is None:\n        raise ImportError_(f\"missing column {name!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n    return row[name]\n\n\ndef _date(text: str, source: str, line: int, formats: tuple[str, ...]):  # noqa: ANN202\n    try:\n        return parse_bank_date(text, formats=formats)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ImportError_(str(exc), source=source, line=line) from None\n\n\ndef read_generic(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"amount\", source, line), decimal_comma=False)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(f\"cannot read the amount {row['amount']!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"date\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,\n            currency=(row.get(\"currency\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=squash(row.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"iban\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef read_ing(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag (EUR)\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(\n                f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag (EUR)']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n            )\n        direction = _field(row, \"Af Bij\", source, line).strip()\n        if direction not in (\"Af\", \"Bij\"):\n            raise ImportError_(f\"Af Bij must be Af or Bij, not {direction!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        name = squash(_field(row, \"Naam / Omschrijving\", source, line))\n        notes = strip_reference(row.get(\"Mededelingen\", \"\"))\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y%m%d\",)),\n            amount=-amount if direction == \"Af\" else amount,\n            currency=\"EUR\",\n            description=f\"{name} {notes}\".strip(),\n            counterparty=name,\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef _is_balance_line(row: dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n    return (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n\n\ndef read_rabo(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n            continue\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            currency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=strip_reference(row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"Naam tegenpartij\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\nREADERS: dict[str, Reader] = {\"generic\": read_generic, \"ing\": read_ing, \"rabo\": read_rabo}\nDELIMITERS = {\"generic\": \",\", \"ing\": \";\", \"rabo\": \",\"}\n\"\"\"Money amounts: ``Decimal`` values with a currency, rounded to the cent only for display.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom decimal import ROUND_HALF_EVEN, ROUND_HALF_UP, Decimal\n\nCENT = Decimal(\"0.01\")\nHOME_CURRENCY = \"EUR\"\nKNOWN_CURRENCIES = frozenset({\"EUR\", \"USD\", \"GBP\", \"CHF\", \"SEK\", \"DKK\", \"NOK\", \"PLN\", \"JPY\"})\nZERO_DECIMAL_CURRENCIES = frozenset({\"JPY\"})\n\n\ndef check_currency(code: str) -> str:\n    code = code.strip().upper()\n    if code not in KNOWN_CURRENCIES:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown currency {code!r}\")\n    return code\n\n\ndef round_cents(amount: Decimal, *, bankers: bool = False) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to the cent: half up for display, half even (``bankers``) for interest.\"\"\"\n\n    return amount.quantize(CENT, rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN if bankers else ROUND_HALF_UP)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True, order=True)\nclass Money:\n    amount: Decimal\n    currency: str = HOME_CURRENCY\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(self.amount, Decimal):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Money needs a Decimal amount, not {type(self.amount).__name__}\")\n        object.__setattr__(self, \"currency\", check_currency(self.currency))\n\n    def __add__(self, other: Money) -> Money:\n        self._same_currency(other)\n        return Money(self.amount + other.amount, self.currency)\n\n    def __sub__(self, other: Money) -> Money:\n        self._same_currency(other)\n        return Money(self.amount - other.amount, self.currency)\n\n    def __neg__(self) -> Money:\n        return Money(-self.amount, self.currency)\n\n    def __mul__(self, factor: Decimal | int) -> Money:\n        return Money(self.amount * Decimal(factor), self.currency)\n\n    def _same_currency(self, other: Money) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(other, Money):\n            raise TypeError(f\"cannot combine Money with {type(other).__name__}\")\n        if other.currency != self.currency:\n            raise ValueError(f\"cannot combine {self.currency} with {other.currency}\")\n\n    @property\n    def is_zero(self) -> bool:\n        return self.amount == 0\n\n    def rounded(self) -> Money:\n        places = Decimal(\"1\") if self.currency in ZERO_DECIMAL_CURRENCIES else CENT\n        return Money(self.amount.quantize(places, rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP), self.currency)\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        value = self.rounded().amount\n        if self.currency in ZERO_DECIMAL_CURRENCIES:\n            return f\"{value:,.0f} {self.currency}\"\n        return f\"{value:,.2f} {self.currency}\"\n\n\ndef total(values: list[Money], currency: str = HOME_CURRENCY) -> Money:\n    \"\"\"The sum of ``values`` (all in ``currency``); zero for an empty list.\"\"\"\n\n    result = Money(Decimal(\"0\"), currency)\n    for value in values:\n        result = result + value\n    return result\n\"\"\"A transaction: one line of a bank statement, after import.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Transaction:\n    \"\"\"Money moving into (positive ``amount``) or out of (negative) an asset or liability\n    ``account``, in that account's statement currency. ``category`` is the income or expense\n    account it belongs to (``None`` until categorised).\"\"\"\n\n    account: str\n    booked: date\n    amount: Decimal\n    currency: str\n    description: str\n    counterparty: str = \"\"\n    counter_iban: str | None = None\n    category: str | None = None\n    source: str = \"\"  # \"<file>:<line>\" it was imported from\n    tags: frozenset[str] = field(default_factory=frozenset)\n\n    @property\n    def fingerprint(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Stable identity for de-duplication: the same statement line imported twice.\"\"\"\n\n        key = \"|\".join(\n            [\n                self.account,\n                self.booked.isoformat(),\n                str(self.amount),\n                self.currency,\n                self.description.strip().lower(),\n                (self.counter_iban or \"\").upper(),\n            ]\n        )\n        return hashlib.sha256(key.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\n\n    @property\n    def is_income(self) -> bool:\n        return self.amount > 0\n\n    def categorised(self, category: str) -> Transaction:\n        return replace(self, category=category)\n\n    def tagged(self, *tags: str) -> Transaction:\n        return replace(self, tags=self.tags | frozenset(tags))\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, object]:\n        return {\n            \"account\": self.account,\n            \"booked\": self.booked.isoformat(),\n            \"amount\": None if self.amount is None else str(self.amount),\n            \"currency\": self.currency,\n            \"description\": self.description,\n            \"counterparty\": self.counterparty,\n            \"counter_iban\": self.counter_iban,\n            \"category\": self.category,\n            \"source\": self.source,\n            \"tags\": sorted(self.tags),\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: dict[str, object]) -> Transaction:\n        raw = data.get(\"amount\")\n        return cls(\n            account=str(data[\"account\"]),\n            booked=date.fromisoformat(str(data[\"booked\"])),\n            amount=None if raw is None else Decimal(str(raw)),  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            currency=str(data[\"currency\"]),\n            description=str(data.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=str(data.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=data.get(\"counter_iban\") or None,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            category=data.get(\"category\") or None,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            source=str(data.get(\"source\", \"\")),\n            tags=frozenset(data.get(\"tags\") or []),  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        )\n\"\"\"The journal: every imported transaction, de-duplicated, in booking order.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom collections.abc import Iterable, Iterator\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.accounts import Chart, Kind\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import LedgerError\nfrom ledgerly.core.periods import Period\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\n\n\nclass Journal:\n    def __init__(self, chart: Chart | None = None) -> None:\n        self.chart = chart or Chart()\n        self._entries: list[Transaction] = []\n        self._seen: set[str] = set()\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\n        return len(self._entries)\n\n    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n        return iter(sorted(self._entries, key=lambda t: (t.booked, t.account, t.source)))\n\n    def add(self, transaction: Transaction) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Add a transaction; ``False`` (and nothing added) when it is already in the journal.\"\"\"\n\n        account = self.chart.get(transaction.account)\n        if account.kind.is_category:\n            raise LedgerError(f\"{account.id} is a category, not an account money is kept in\")\n        if account.closed:\n            raise LedgerError(f\"account {account.id} is closed\")\n        if transaction.category is not None and transaction.category not in self.chart:\n            raise LedgerError(f\"no category {transaction.category!r}\")\n        if transaction.fingerprint in self._seen:\n            return False\n        self._seen.add(transaction.fingerprint)\n        self._entries.append(transaction)\n        return True\n\n    def extend(self, transactions: Iterable[Transaction]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Add many; returns ``(added, duplicates)``.\"\"\"\n\n        added = duplicates = 0\n        for transaction in transactions:\n            if self.add(transaction):\n                added += 1\n            else:\n                duplicates += 1\n        return added, duplicates\n\n    def replace_all(self, transactions: Iterable[Transaction]) -> None:\n        self._entries, self._seen = [], set()\n        self.extend(transactions)\n\n    def in_period(self, period: Period) -> list[Transaction]:\n        return [t for t in self if period.contains(t.booked)]\n\n    def for_account(self, account_id: str) -> list[Transaction]:\n        self.chart.get(account_id)\n        return [t for t in self if t.account == account_id]\n\n    def first_and_last(self) -> tuple[date, date] | None:\n        dates = [t.booked for t in self._entries]\n        return (min(dates), max(dates)) if dates else None\n\n    def by_category(self, period: Period) -> dict[str, list[Transaction]]:\n        grouped: dict[str, list[Transaction]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for transaction in self.in_period(period):\n            grouped[transaction.category or \"uncategorised\"].append(transaction)\n        return dict(grouped)\n\n    def money_accounts(self) -> list[str]:\n        kinds = (Kind.ASSET, Kind.LIABILITY)\n        return [a.id for a in self.chart.all() if a.kind in kinds]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
